A pool for each kind of mapped batch: transform and filemeta

The mapped batches of an indexing run are all queued at once when the DAG's
task limits allow it, but a worker runs only as many as it has processes. A
batch that waits in the broker's queue longer than the scheduler's
task_queued_timeout (600 s by default) is retried and then failed; a long run
with many batches per process loses the batches at the back. A pool with as
many slots as the worker's processes keeps the rest scheduled, not queued,
where the timeout does not apply, and shows the limit in Airflow's UI. The
pools must exist; the modama search stack creates both (init-airflow.sh) and
the transform worker sets `transform` to its process count at start.

Against metadata-warehouse v1.10.0; applied with `patch -p1` in the image build
(modama search stack, warehouse-airflow.Dockerfile; change cpu-budget, D6).

diff --git a/airflow/dags/transform_index.py b/airflow/dags/transform_index.py
